  "summary": "Lightwell Security Advisory: pyjwt 2.10.1+rhlw.1",
  "details": "Red Hat Lightwell has released pyjwt 2.10.1+rhlw.1 with backported fixes for CVE-2026-102274, CVE-2026-102269, CVE-2026-32597, CVE-2026-101918, CVE-2026-48523, CVE-2026-101917, CVE-2026-48522, CVE-2026-102267, CVE-2026-48525, CVE-2026-102271, CVE-2026-102270, CVE-2026-102268, CVE-2026-48526, and CVE-2026-102275.\n\nCVE-2026-102274: PyJWT: Malformed RSA JWK aborts parsing of an entire JWK Set\n\nCVE-2026-102269: PyJWT: Non-canonical signature segments enable raw-token revocation bypass\n\nCVE-2026-32597: PyJWT accepts unknown `crit` header extensions (RFC 7515 \u00a74.1.11 MUST violation)\n\nCVE-2026-101918: PyJWT: Unauthenticated RecursionError DoS in pre-verification payload parse (PyJWKClient.get_signing_key_from_jwt / verify_signature=False)\n\nCVE-2026-48523: PyJWT: Algorithm allow-list bypass when decoding with `PyJWK` / `PyJWKClient` keys\n\nCVE-2026-101917: PyJWT: PyJWKClient still amplifies unauthenticated JWKS fetches on unknown kid values (incomplete fix of CVE-2026-48524)\n\nCVE-2026-48522: PyJWKClient: missing scheme allowlist enables SSRF + token forgery via file://, ftp://, data: schemes\n\nCVE-2026-102267: PyJWT: PyJWKClient follows redirects when fetching JWKS\n\nCVE-2026-48525: PyJWT: Unauthenticated DoS via unbounded Base64URL decoding of unused payload segment in b64=false detached JWS\n\nCVE-2026-102271: PyJWT: Public keys in DER form are accepted as HMAC secrets, bypassing the CVE-2022-29217 guard\n\nCVE-2026-102270: PyJWT: ReDoS vulnerability when calling the `is_pem_format` function.\n\nCVE-2026-102268: PyJWT: Asymmetric-PEM detection bypass: whitespace/line-ending-mutated public keys skip the HS/asymmetric confusion guard\n\nCVE-2026-48526: PyJWT: Public-key JWK accepted as HMAC secret enables forged HS256 tokens when mixed families are allowed\n\nCVE-2026-102275: PyJWT accepts inconsistent OKP x/d JWKs, causing public/private key identity confusion\n\nThis patched artifact is a drop-in replacement for pyjwt 2.10.1 from PyPI.",
